            <div xml:id="d91">

                <pb facs="0238" n="110" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg110"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.4212Anti-War/42</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Canada</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Baldwin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ottawa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17,
                        1928</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received July 19.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 529</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Legation’s telegrams No.
                    155 of July 17, 2 p.m., and No. 156 of July 17, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="95"
                        xml:id="d91-f1"/> I have the honor to transmit herewith enclosed a copy of a
                    note received from W. L. Mackenzie King, Secretary of State for External
                    Affairs, stating that His Majesty’s Government in Canada cordially accepts the
                    Treaty as revised and is prepared to participate in its signature.</p>
                <pb facs="0239" n="111" xml:id="pg111"/>
                <p>Since the Canadian Government does not desire that its reply be published before
                    that of the British Government, it has been agreed that the Canadian reply will
                    be released for publication in the morning newspapers of Thursday, July 19.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">La Verne Baldwin</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d91-a1.xml" xpointer="d91-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
